    {
      "title": "List and Tuple Operations and Costs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "List and Tuple Operations and Costs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. List = dynamic array",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cost",
                "Operations"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:O(1)}",
                  "`lst[i]`, `len`, `append`, `pop()` (amortized)"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:O(n)}",
                  "`insert(0,x)`, `pop(0)`, `remove(x)`, `x in lst`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Methods and sorting",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`append(x)` adds one item; `extend(it)` adds each item of `it`",
                "`insert(i,x)` puts x at index i; `remove(x)` deletes the first match",
                "`pop(i=-1)` removes and returns an item",
                "`sort()` works ==in place== and returns `None`",
                "`sorted(it)` returns a **new** list",
                "Stable ==Timsort==, O(n log n)",
                "`key=len` or `key=lambda t: t[1]` picks the field; `reverse=True` flips"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "pairs = [('a', 3), ('b', 1), ('c', 2)]",
                "print(sorted(pairs, key=lambda t: t[1], reverse=True))",
                "print(pairs.sort())"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[('a', 3), ('c', 2), ('b', 1)]",
                "None"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Tuples",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Immutable, fixed size: ==records==, multiple return values, dict keys",
                "Unpack: `a, *rest = (1, 2, 3)` gives `rest == [2, 3]`",
                "One item needs a comma: `(1,)`; `(1)` is just an int"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pops at both ends",
              "text": "Use `collections.deque` for ==O(1)== pops at both ends; `list.pop(0)` is O(n)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
